# Cloudflare Email Routing — desired state for every domain you own.
# Read by scripts/cf-email-routing.sh (plan / apply / status).
# Full explanation: docs/03-cloudflare-email-routing.md
#
#   cp deploy/cloudflare/email-routing.conf.example deploy/cloudflare/email-routing.conf
#
# One rule per line, whitespace-separated:
#
#   <zone>          <address>                 <action>  [<target>]
#
#   zone     the Cloudflare zone (apex domain) the rule lives in
#   address  full address (local@domain), or * for the zone's catch-all
#   action   worker   -> target is the Worker name (e.g. singlestack-inbound-mail)
#            forward  -> target is a destination mailbox (verified once per account)
#            drop     -> no target; silently discard
#
# The script only creates and updates the rules listed here. It never deletes
# rules it doesn't know about; it lists them as "unmanaged" so you can decide.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.

# ── brand 1 ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
example.com      support@example.com      worker   singlestack-inbound-mail
example.com      reply@example.com        worker   singlestack-inbound-mail
example.com      hello@example.com        forward  you@your-mailbox.example
example.com      dmarc@example.com        forward  you@your-mailbox.example
example.com      *                        drop

# ── brand 2 (same Worker, same Chatwoot; add a matching inbox in Chatwoot) ─
example.org      support@example.org      worker   singlestack-inbound-mail
example.org      *                        forward  you@your-mailbox.example

# ── a domain that only forwards (no support desk) ─────────────────────────
example.net      *                        forward  you@your-mailbox.example
